<article class="card post"><h3>True Darkness</h3><p class="verse">Oblivion..<br>A dance caused by trembles beneath my skin<br>A tale not told but sung with cries<br>A void filled with empty shreds of hope<br><br>My heart shines as a candle in a vast black room<br>Bound by reality of being changed in the abyss<br>I found myself breathing in countless shadows<br>Shadows that filled my lungs with a raging vortex<br>I remained bright as I burned away<br>Each passing moment felt nearer to the end<br>Like a clock that ticked sounds of decay<br>The end is near and yet life remained in a loop<br>An endless torture,<br>Thorns pierced through weeping skin<br>How wicked could the shadows be<br>To be shunned and cast away as a forsaken folktale<br><br>The tide between countless shadows waged a war<br>Like an armada the ghosts fled across the room<br>How could a simple flame breathe through a sea of black?<br>Alone with only myself to keep me warm<br>The hands of the abyss clutched onto my neck<br>And like smoldering rocks despair sank down my throat<br>A bitter taste of pain stung with bitter haste<br><br>My heart afraid of the thread beneath the wax<br>Wax that covered my heart as gentle walls<br>Fear lurked through the corners of the abyss<br>Shatter my bones like a sanctioned mirror<br>Could I ever see my reflection as a burning flame?<br>Or would I see a reflection of a passing candle?<br>Pitch black sorrows may seem true and still<br>Still as the silence that strayed into the dark<br>Shimmers of sparks rattle from time to time<br>It was only a flame burning through the pain<br><br>Could a flame shed tears?<br>Or would those very tears extinguish me?<br>Only fools had forgotten hopes when nothing feels real<br>So I remained that fool like a king’s court jester</p><div class="act"><button class="like" data-k="p1"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ih"/></svg><span>0</span></button><a class="tipb" title="Tip jar: leave a small tip for this poem" href="https://paypal.me/MikaaeelArnold001" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ijar"/></svg>Tip</a></div></article>
<article class="card post"><h3>A friend I never had</h3><p class="sub">Would the world remain vibrant without you?</p><p class="verse">It was your presence that delivered a warm breeze through the atmosphere—<br>A presence so intense it chased away the fear.<br>Your smile, deep as dawn, awakened every living thing within me.<br>You’re an embodiment of illumination; believe me, you’re the key.<br><br>A friend who stood as a knight in shining armour,<br>A friend who lifted the veil from a dark world without glamour.<br>A stranger? Once, yes, but eventually manifested as my one and only guardian.<br>My protector, my elevator, my conqueror; when I shed tears, you’re the one easing my pain.<br><br>The pet names you call me are sweet and elegant, yet I weaken every time you say my name.<br>You’re the one who carried me through tough times, dragging me to the light even when I’d complain.<br>You remain a stain intertwined with my brain—I wouldn’t want it any other way.<br>Each time I giggle in a room of silence, I wish you were here.<br>I wish goodbyes never existed, so you could stay.</p><div class="act"><button class="like" data-k="p2"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ih"/></svg><span>0</span></button><a class="tipb" title="Tip jar: leave a small tip for this poem" href="https://paypal.me/MikaaeelArnold001" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ijar"/></svg>Tip</a></div></article>
<article class="card post"><h3>A journey set out towards…</h3><p class="verse">Towards the sunset.<br>A place filled with citrus –<br>Orange beams of light that held my hand.<br>Even though I was down, I got back up.<br>I wish to be a part of you,<br>to be your friend,<br>to be …<br>Well, only time can tell.<br>How I waited for a rainbow through an endless rain.<br>The pain –<br>stay strong, little one.<br>One day you’ll beat a rhythm filled with joy.<br>We will dance again.<br>For now we remain the same,<br>but we could still dance through the rain.<br>One day we’ll hold hands again.</p><div class="act"><button class="like" data-k="p3"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ih"/></svg><span>0</span></button><a class="tipb" title="Tip jar: leave a small tip for this poem" href="https://paypal.me/MikaaeelArnold001" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ijar"/></svg>Tip</a></div></article>
<article class="card post"><h3>A touch of poison that became my obsession</h3><p class="sub">Was my body just another playground?</p><p class="cw">CONTENT NOTE · Adult themes</p><p class="verse">What was it that I saw in his crystal blue gaze that had me pulled into a void of lust.<br>How could a stranger seem familiar? His kindness brushed off like delusions from my past.<br>A rose he was that I plucked from a field stained in white by a horde of lilies stacked in entity.<br>Like eye candy, my eyes watered as my lips slipped beneath my teeth, I seemed all willy-nilly.<br><br>An addiction that kept me from fading into the howling shadows of the night.<br>Poison that petrified the urge to resist, temptation stood tall as a lamented blight.<br>“Mmmm!”, my arms reached out as my hands crawled steadily clinging to the comfort of pleasure.<br>Pinned down as a slave chained by the cold metals of ecstasy, his sword pierced through my soul without measure.<br><br>Like waves that washed over my skin, his touch slithered a faint breeze across my breast.<br>This was not love and yet he had my heart beating drums behind the cage of my chest.<br>Like serpents we tangled each other, turning and tossing like raging rapids between the sheets.<br>It was pure bliss as he held my hand escorting my orgasms through a river that led to my feet.<br><br>If I could, I would, another chance is all I need to drown in his poisonous touch.<br>He tossed me aside as if my body had been forsaken by pleasure-less pleasure, still as a ticking watch.<br>A man that deemed himself worthy of conquering Eve after devouring her forbidden fruit.<br>In the end I remained a sandbox for a child to play in, how lust hid behind a deceitful truth.</p><div class="act"><button class="like" data-k="p4"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ih"/></svg><span>0</span></button><a class="tipb" title="Tip jar: leave a small tip for this poem" href="https://paypal.me/MikaaeelArnold001" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ijar"/></svg>Tip</a></div></article>
<article class="card post"><h3>The cheater that clings to me</h3><p class="sub">Is forgiveness all that we have?</p><p class="verse">My soul torn to shreds by the very words you left behind.<br>Abandoned by truth and trust, forsaken in mind.<br>Blind and yet kind, I try to move on from the chains of regret that kept me confined.<br>How bonds shattered into a million fragments form a broken mirror—a reflection that couldn’t unwind.<br><br>Were my tears not enough? All I ever received were empty sorries filled with mockery.<br>Anxiety: the only friend that never betrayed me, the only friend that stood beside me.<br>Each time you smiled, the air filled with miasma, clogging the very breath I seek.<br>Bleak, wondering if I’d ever hold your hand the same way again—how you left so quick.<br><br>Each kiss I received stained my heart with countless threats from another woman’s touch.<br>It wasn’t much—the love I received whenever you arrived smelling of perfume, it was just a hunch.<br>And yet, that was a lie I told myself to find the love that once loved me for who I am.<br>Who’s to blame? Each night I drown in the fear that stained our chamber, but I could never complain.<br><br>How could you cherish flowers in a withered garden filled with grey hints of despair?<br>I do care; I’m only human. Why is it that every time I forgive you, I receive thorns that fill the air?<br>Why does my heart never learn? Why does my soul cling to false hopes and dreams?<br>At the end, I could never love another man as much as the one who left a kiss of incompatible compassion—to what means?</p><div class="act"><button class="like" data-k="p5"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ih"/></svg><span>0</span></button><a class="tipb" title="Tip jar: leave a small tip for this poem" href="https://paypal.me/MikaaeelArnold001" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ijar"/></svg>Tip</a></div></article>
<article class="card post"><h3>Were we ever … close?</h3><p class="verse">Is it me?<br>Am I really the one to blame?<br>The silent clocks ticked muted tocks.<br>Your voice that once illuminated my heart now shades it.<br>The memories that lingered started to fade –<br>Bonds bound by broken breathless breaths.<br><br>Why did you change?<br>Was my purpose fulfilled as a tool used and tossed away?<br>Why does it hurt this way?<br>Questions asked by numbers instead of words.<br>I get it now.<br>The void that showered your grace gave place,<br>Upon a space that I filled with kind gestures and tepid talks.<br>And yet I remain as steady as a beam that stood as your support.<br><br>Watched as I did, stood actively in the midst.<br>Your happiness – the only joy I found in a friend.<br>I reached out to lend a hand.<br>Lumps of carbon that filled my lungs as your silence thickened.<br>How ironic,<br>I thought maybe I found the missing part of me.<br>But in the end you proved I’m not your missing piece.</p><div class="act"><button class="like" data-k="p6"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ih"/></svg><span>0</span></button><a class="tipb" title="Tip jar: leave a small tip for this poem" href="https://paypal.me/MikaaeelArnold001" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ijar"/></svg>Tip</a></div></article>
<article class="card post"><h3>It hurts</h3><p class="cw">CONTENT NOTE · Themes of depression and suicide</p><p class="verse">It hurts ..<br>It hurts so much.<br>I blame myself every minute, every second.<br>Why was it me born in this life?<br>I hate the person I am.<br>I hate the way I smile and say it’s ok each time.<br>I hate the way I tell myself it’s ok.<br>I hate that…<br>What am I?<br>Am I just not meant to be happy?<br>Why should I feel this way every single day?<br>Was it fate that brought me here?<br>Or was I destined to suffer for eternity?<br><br>My tears stood frozen glistening through the dark as I stared at shadows that crowd my room.<br>Every thought betrayed me and every feeling consumed me, maybe it will end very soon.<br>The white lie that keeps a bladed smile upon my face –<br>daggers always get the best of me.<br>Why do I cheer myself with cheers from a crowd-less crowd?<br>Maybe death would be the key I seek.<br>Even if I pass the world would remain blissful without me,<br>with zero worth it’s easy to replace me.<br>I know I’m not the best and never expected to be a hero,<br>shamed by destiny to be the villain.<br><br>Why can’t I be happy? Is it because the scars ruined the image of my heart?<br>I barely recognise myself anymore, the countless masks I wear to keep the world happy.<br>All my life I was a professional actor and yet not once have I received an award.<br>I just wanted to smile a truthful smile.<br>I guess some of us aren’t meant to… I get it.<br>It’s ok, I’ll make it… And yet my tears keep coming back.<br>Like chains binding my very soul, the tortures that trampled my tepid heart with tyrannical taunts.<br><br>Sometimes my tears feel warm and sometimes it feels like a blade slashing down my cheeks.<br>What is pain to me?<br>Pain is my friend that never left my side, the one that crushed my hand and suffocated my heart –<br>Over and over and over again.<br>Maybe one day I’ll be free from this.<br>Can I really be free from this pain when every memory haunts me as the demons in my dreams?<br>Every nightmare felt like never ending lucid dreams – demons that barged in uninvited.<br>I wish maybe everything could end, and my emptiness from the world place smiles and joys to everyone around.</p><div class="act"><button class="like" data-k="p7"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ih"/></svg><span>0</span></button><a class="tipb" title="Tip jar: leave a small tip for this poem" href="https://paypal.me/MikaaeelArnold001" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ijar"/></svg>Tip</a></div></article>
<article class="card post"><h3>Sorrow that always knocks on my door</h3><p class="verse">Thoughts beheaded by a curse of oppressed vows made by whips that lashed my love away.<br>A cocktail made from pain, sorrow and revenge, drunk from a demonic drink kissed by the shadows.<br>A gaze that froze time, cold as the night sky lonely without sparkles to twinkle my beast.<br>Dragged by what could have been my fear and yet it was chained humour I sought to find.<br>My thoughts afraid of me, a quiet mind that echoes darkness in a void of muted voice.<br>Disgusted by the personalities that kept me human, why is death shy upon my prey.<br>Poison that kept me breathing in a world not meant for the heart I had to be gifted with.<br><br>All I know is pain<br>This was never a game<br>Thrown by hurt, judged and yet I remain<br>False with a smile that complements the rain<br>Why would you say my name<br>To have me drown in a drain<br>We’re not the same<br>The journey of cries of a little child in my brain<br>Who do I blame?<br>Trust was never a place from where I came<br>How do I maintain<br>Hands that itched then irked for regretful fame<br>My heart set ablaze like a burning flame<br>Why do I complain<br>To an empty void that kept me insane<br>Dragged by shame<br>A heart that bled the same as my brain left a stain<br>What was your aim?<br>Yet I love the hurt that I had to claim<br>This is my terrain<br>A valley of my demons meant to contain<br>The truth that never held me a campaign</p><div class="act"><button class="like" data-k="p8"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ih"/></svg><span>0</span></button><a class="tipb" title="Tip jar: leave a small tip for this poem" href="https://paypal.me/MikaaeelArnold001" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ijar"/></svg>Tip</a></div></article>
<article class="card post"><h3>Could I still be the same without you?</h3><p class="cw">CONTENT NOTE · Themes of self-harm and suicide</p><p class="verse">Underneath a violet moon twinkled my tears that glimmer as crystals dancing through the air.<br>Clinging to my heart as it bleeds an endless river, the tighter I hold the more my pain reverts its glare.<br>A nightly confinement left me dancing with the shadows that I fear – someone save me.<br>I tried to breathe as my breath betrayed the very lungs that guided my heart to a deep black sea.<br><br>The silence behind screams shattered emotions that echoed throughout a void that filled the room.<br>“Why did it have to be this way?”, my hand choked the very thoughts that left my mind.<br>They said I was crazy, a lunatic, a girl that lost her way through a realm of forgetting memories.<br>Maybe I am, maybe those words carried a weight of truth that buried a song without melodies.<br><br>How my eyes glistened towards the stars that wish to feel my pain, yet I wished for my end.<br>“I wish I could be with you”, if only I could cross over the walls of life and death – only a message I wish to send.<br>As I float over a tepid crimson pool my heart withers away as if autumn entered my very soul.<br>Currents flowing from my wrist as steady streams washing away the emptiness that once filled my hole.<br><br>Spirits that touch the life I once thought was untouchable, the winds called with a lovely cry.<br>A meditation still and bitter as I share the ground medication that led to temptation – I could fly.<br>The very air I once knew became a stranger to me, gentle skin that turned pale and cold as ice.<br>“At least we’ll see each other again”, the last tear drop I felt so warm with life felt so nice.</p><div class="act"><button class="like" data-k="p9"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ih"/></svg><span>0</span></button><a class="tipb" title="Tip jar: leave a small tip for this poem" href="https://paypal.me/MikaaeelArnold001" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ijar"/></svg>Tip</a></div></article>
<article class="card post"><h3>A rose free as a stolen soul</h3><p class="cw">CONTENT NOTE · Themes of death</p><p class="verse">It called my name as if fate brought us together.<br>Panting from the journey that brought me here, my heart beats a calming fear.<br>Tailed by anxiety and tragic horrors that wish to cage my freedom away.<br>Should I not have the right to play?<br>A little girl in a world that seemed gentle in each and every way.<br>I couldn’t stay.<br>Ran I did for the beauty that my heart desires, not wealth, not fame, just peace in a little sandbox.<br><br>Could I still play?<br>Why, why, why!<br>Blood bled a ballet that bestowed a dance banned by brutal behaviour.<br>How death called for a favour.<br>All that I had was my smile that kept me going, and here we are in a garden of my passing.<br>An arrow that pierced through my tiny waist – if only it was Cupid that shot me.<br>Free at last as I took my last few breaths that held my hand through the dangers clinging to my death.<br><br>The sky blissful in every way, leaden grey clouds and a withered sun.<br>A view that graced my final moments.<br>Why did it have to end like this?<br>In a garden of lilies stood one perfect rose, shy and unapologetic crimson through the white.<br>I laid my head next to it as my blood stained the ground in a sea of red.<br>I accept this beautiful death, it was as if we were destined to meet.<br>My last moment with you and yet I wish it could have been our first of many beginnings.</p><div class="act"><button class="like" data-k="p10"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ih"/></svg><span>0</span></button><a class="tipb" title="Tip jar: leave a small tip for this poem" href="https://paypal.me/MikaaeelArnold001" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ijar"/></svg>Tip</a></div></article>
<article class="card post"><h3>The last sunset that left bitter to my grace</h3><p class="verse">The air crimson in a way and yet stained by citrus outside yellow agenda.<br>Winds blew a graceful goodbye as the sun found its way in a realm of departure.<br>A timeless foundation that held day firm as the night began to fall.<br>An adventure to what felt like forever and yet it was a moment that could last after all.<br>Birds sang songs that complemented the dancing leaves through the air.<br>A duet sung by day and night as they exchanged vows – the moon not in sight felt near.<br><br>Through it all her hair stood out as a thorn with a flower’s identity, how beauty felt so sad.<br>Was I mad? How could I be mad at a doll that stood between here and there, gone yet she may stay.<br>Don’t stray away from peace that held our hearts chained by cold metals of reality.<br>“Hold me, don’t chase me”, screams that betrayed her gaze as crystals shed down her cheeks.<br>My eyes complemented the sorrows with a lovely cry, a smile that held my heart warm.<br>From the darkness that sought to conquer our bonds, blinded by light that took her form.<br><br>Alas, what was love in the end when it couldn’t save the hearts of two broken souls.<br>Why did it feel like a void filled with happiness while I bled shades of despair?<br>Don’t look at me with a tepid glare, the comfort of your hazel wood left roots of memories beneath my skin.<br>Never has a simple goodbye felt so aggravating towards my mind as it sparked a dilemma.<br>As the night came, the abyss of departure sank a rock within my sea of love – I understood and I cared.<br>Was it me or was it you? How did we end up in a place where dreams and memories roamed the air?</p><div class="act"><button class="like" data-k="p11"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ih"/></svg><span>0</span></button><a class="tipb" title="Tip jar: leave a small tip for this poem" href="https://paypal.me/MikaaeelArnold001" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ijar"/></svg>Tip</a></div></article>
<article class="card post"><h3>Stay</h3><p class="verse">It wasn’t what it seemed,<br>Citrus winds through your sunless absence.<br>Tides washed upon my gentle skin – where do I begin?<br>Dewdrops over the gaze that remembered your smile.<br>You were kind and yet I remained blind.<br>How do I rewind the days that held our bonds?<br>Stay –<br>Tears of bitter burial beneath broken borders.<br>My heart calls to an echo that never reached back to me.<br>If only I could hear your voice once more,<br>I sang the songs you loved to remember your dance.<br>Melodies that preserved your entity within my walls.<br>The halls kept extending to a journey-less journey.<br>And yet my vision fixated on the very light that resembled you.<br>You remain the antidote<br>To my poisonous lonesome</p><div class="act"><button class="like" data-k="p12"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ih"/></svg><span>0</span></button><a class="tipb" title="Tip jar: leave a small tip for this poem" href="https://paypal.me/MikaaeelArnold001" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ijar"/></svg>Tip</a></div></article>
<article class="card post"><h3>Grief with a tyrannical smile</h3><p class="verse">Come back!<br><br>His name stained my identity,<br>Side by side across broken roads.<br>Healing without treatment,<br>Was laughter ever the best medicine?<br>How funny it is to chuckle at my pain.<br>Is this funny?<br>Questions that puzzled my soul.<br>Sharing a smirk with misery<br>Or is that an apology?<br>Strands of forgotten love linger through the air<br>Did you not care that it was not far?<br>Yes, to me.<br>Why didn’t you choose me?<br>A broken piece from what was complete<br>I thought you and I had a connection through prayer<br>But it was only mixed signals from a signal jam<br><br>I hate you!<br><br>Winds of despair blew a gentle breeze<br>As dawn reversed into the night<br>How I was blind<br>But I’m sure it would work out<br>Sticking around like sticky threads<br>And yet why didn’t you love me back<br>Why did you have to leave me?<br>I loved you but that wasn’t enough<br>Like a glass half full and yet half empty.<br>The wisdom, the blessings were they all a lie?<br>Hold me one more time for I’ll never forget you<br>The pillar that kept me strong and bold<br>What have I done to deserve this?<br>Couldn’t it be me and not you… father<br>May you gaze upon your daughter’s tears<br>Keep me safe, as do my memories of you<br>Love you dad<br>May we meet again reincarnated between realms.</p><div class="act"><button class="like" data-k="p13"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ih"/></svg><span>0</span></button><a class="tipb" title="Tip jar: leave a small tip for this poem" href="https://paypal.me/MikaaeelArnold001" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ijar"/></svg>Tip</a></div></article>
<article class="card post"><h3>Shadow walker</h3><p class="sub">The shadows beneath my feet</p><p class="verse">Why hide yourself from the night sky that tossed a veil over a table surrounded by empty chairs?<br>The abyss bloomed within an hour, time that ticks in shades of neon black star dust.<br>Why do you pretend to hate the light when you exist through its dwindling aroma?<br>Or so I say, and yet through the shadows you never existed as if the darkness rejected you from the underworld.<br><br>Was it not you that kept me safe when I ran from your threats?<br>You’ve always been by my side and yet you’ve never been there for me.<br>An actor who pretended to be my friend on a stage shamed by the blight of a silent audience.<br>Sing I may, to sway the way you play muted melodies at bay – shattered notes cracked away.<br><br>Vows made through birth, a priest of light that chained our paths as one.<br>Yet we couldn’t touch hands as if we were never meant to be, so you see how it’s always been you and me.<br>Why do you stare at me as if I’ve lost my sanity to a thief in the winds?<br>Why do you mimic me? Do you not have a destiny of your own desire?<br><br>I tried to let you go to hide the pain away from you, tears that fell from a waterless well.<br>Breathe as I should, wander as I could, a lost soul roaming around false hope and desire.<br>Why don’t you break free? Why do you keep your distance, an inch away from my heart?<br>But at the end my hero, my friend and protector was and always has been my shadow.</p><div class="act"><button class="like" data-k="p14"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ih"/></svg><span>0</span></button><a class="tipb" title="Tip jar: leave a small tip for this poem" href="https://paypal.me/MikaaeelArnold001" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ijar"/></svg>Tip</a></div></article>
<article class="card post"><h3>What hope feels like in an empty void</h3><p class="verse">Love that creeped behind complexity<br>As tepid mist filled the air with ecstasy<br>Our bonds broken and lost through memory<br>Hinged on a path built by sympathy<br>The empathy,<br>How you laughed over my misery<br>My heart pinned to the ground by gravity<br>Flawless flaws strung a rhythm-less melody<br>The consistency<br>You kept crawling into my life flawlessly<br>Lies that persuade my heart with honesty<br>A leap I took fearlessly<br>Love shattered through infinity<br>To be trapped in a loop of broken clarity<br>The sincerity<br>Pitch black were the sparkles of your heart as a fantasy<br>What have I gained through your lustful monopoly<br>As I try to breathe through my anxiety<br>My heart so kind and lost became my enemy<br>Where is your energy<br>A forgotten sanctuary<br>The burden of our trust that weighed on me so heavily<br>A conundrum that erupted my calamity<br>Untold stories were told terribly<br>Illegibly<br>A faded smile twinkles to what we call astrology<br>You abandoned me<br>Was love not meant for my sanity<br>The agony<br>Wasted my time and effort too casually<br>Like scars that remained on my soul for eternity</p><div class="act"><button class="like" data-k="p15"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ih"/></svg><span>0</span></button><a class="tipb" title="Tip jar: leave a small tip for this poem" href="https://paypal.me/MikaaeelArnold001" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ijar"/></svg>Tip</a></div></article>
<article class="card post"><h3>A raindance of a broken soul</h3><p class="sub">It was only the rain that understood my pain.</p><p class="verse">A ballet of rain that danced through the air without a care, a leaden grey sky cried a thousand tears.<br>Thunder that echoed through the cold, neon veins coloured the sky in crystal blue each time they appear.<br>The wind whispered a breeze that swayed the trees to lean back as if they gazed upon showers of illusion.<br>Leaves brushed through the air while the relentless ripples rushed them towards a never ending conclusion.<br><br>Through it all I stood still as if time had a moment to cherish my endless sorrows.<br>The smile that kept me free felt like dilutions devouring my diminished soul – hilarious horrors.<br>The chills – my skin drowned beneath a sea of droplets, it was as if my body couldn’t breathe through it all.<br>And yet I danced to note-less notes, a muted melody that played through roars of the fall.<br><br>Puddles remained unwearied as I skipped around.<br>The splashes of each puddle remained anonymous through the rain as they found their way back to the ground.<br>Around and around I spun, a world that seemed to never end and yet it came to an end.<br>The clouds held a divorcing ceremony as the rain came to a halt, the rays of light could not pretend.<br><br>A rainbow that stood tall in different shades of emotions, how the weather’s personality changed instantly.<br>From a smile that bloomed in liquid form to a frown that illuminated the sky as if it was meant to be.<br>Was it really meant to be? How the sun shined upon my hidden tears and revealed the pain within me.</p><div class="act"><button class="like" data-k="p16"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ih"/></svg><span>0</span></button><a class="tipb" title="Tip jar: leave a small tip for this poem" href="https://paypal.me/MikaaeelArnold001" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic"><use href="#ijar"/></svg>Tip</a></div></article>
